Objective

This lab focused on managing identities and access within Microsoft Entra ID. The exercises introduced the creation and configuration of users, guest accounts, and security groups in Azure.

The lab also demonstrated how organizations manage identity solutions for both internal employees and external collaborators while reducing administrative overhead through group management strategies.

Lab Scenario

The scenario involved configuring a new pre-production lab environment where engineers required access to manage Azure virtual machines and services.

The objectives included:

Provisioning internal users
Inviting external guest users
Creating security groups
Assigning group owners and members
Understanding static and dynamic group memberships

The environment was managed using the Azure portal and Microsoft Entra ID.

